WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.093 --> 00:00:01.277
- So my name is Jason Quinn,

00:00:01.277 --> 00:00:03.018
chef/owner of Playground, Playground 2.0

00:00:03.018 --> 00:00:04.110
where we're standing right now

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:06.617
and Dough Exchange our bakery next door.

00:00:06.617 --> 00:00:08.707
Today we are all about foie gras.

00:00:08.707 --> 00:00:10.564
We're going to show
four different varieties

00:00:10.564 --> 00:00:12.422
of how it can be prepared or served.

00:00:12.422 --> 00:00:14.279
And hopefully take some foie virgins

00:00:14.279 --> 00:00:16.230
and turn them into believers.

00:00:16.230 --> 00:00:18.109
(accordion music)

00:00:29.976 --> 00:00:32.040
You look at the way that
foie gras is produced

00:00:32.040 --> 00:00:34.780
in Turkey or Hungary where
ducks are nailed down

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:36.266
through their feet and they never move

00:00:36.266 --> 00:00:37.296
their whole lives, and they have

00:00:37.296 --> 00:00:38.599
a tube down their throat, just fed.

00:00:38.599 --> 00:00:39.532
It's pure evil.

00:00:39.532 --> 00:00:40.600
Where we get our foie gras from

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.434
these are ducks that run wild.

00:00:42.434 --> 00:00:44.059
They're not in cages.

00:00:44.059 --> 00:00:45.871
As a restaurant owner, it is our place

00:00:45.871 --> 00:00:47.566
to provide things that people want to eat.

00:00:47.566 --> 00:00:49.353
My problem with the ban of it

00:00:49.353 --> 00:00:50.886
was not that foie gras was legal.

00:00:50.886 --> 00:00:52.697
It's that someone was telling you

00:00:52.697 --> 00:00:54.229
what you could or couldn't eat.

00:00:54.229 --> 00:00:55.483
And that was what I felt was the reason

00:00:55.483 --> 00:00:56.923
to stand up against it,

00:00:56.923 --> 00:00:58.170
is more about the fact that people should

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:59.137
be able to eat what they like,

00:00:59.137 --> 00:01:00.252
and if you don't want to eat it,

00:01:00.252 --> 00:01:01.923
no one's ever going to make do it.

00:01:01.923 --> 00:01:04.570
So this is smoked foie gras
with a little bit of radish,

00:01:04.570 --> 00:01:07.240
watercress, bourbon
barrel-aged maple syrup.

00:01:07.240 --> 00:01:08.448
- [Tester] He said to pick it up,

00:01:08.448 --> 00:01:09.678
I don't I'm going to pick it up.

00:01:09.678 --> 00:01:10.657
- This is like okay.

00:01:10.657 --> 00:01:11.651
- Mm!

00:01:11.651 --> 00:01:12.752
- Wow!

00:01:12.752 --> 00:01:15.494
- I have to say like I
wanted to not like this.

00:01:15.494 --> 00:01:17.150
Like I really wanted to not like it,

00:01:17.150 --> 00:01:19.170
but it's kind of awesome.

00:01:19.170 --> 00:01:21.051
- It's both salty and sweet.

00:01:21.051 --> 00:01:23.642
- I don't know how to
explain the foie part of it.

00:01:24.404 --> 00:01:27.518
It's almost like a animal butter.

00:01:27.518 --> 00:01:29.863
- Yeah, yeah it's like animal butter.

00:01:29.863 --> 00:01:31.604
- Animal butter, yeah.
- Yeah, it's creamy sort of.

00:01:31.604 --> 00:01:33.090
- What now it's raw?

00:01:33.090 --> 00:01:34.158
- [Jason] Just cold smoked.

00:01:34.158 --> 00:01:35.691
- I feel like if I would
have remembered that

00:01:35.691 --> 00:01:37.688
when I ate I would have
been like freaked out.

00:01:37.688 --> 00:01:39.174
But it was so good.

00:01:39.174 --> 00:01:40.358
- Are we ready for the next course?

00:01:40.358 --> 00:01:41.635
- [Tester] Yeah!
- [Jason] Yeah?

00:01:41.635 --> 00:01:45.919
- [Jason] This is one is
foie gras with rhubarb jam

00:01:45.919 --> 00:01:47.414
and gingersnap cookies.

00:01:47.414 --> 00:01:49.295
And this is called torchon.

00:01:49.295 --> 00:01:50.641
I think when it's cold like this

00:01:50.641 --> 00:01:52.778
you get a lot of the
subtlety of the flavor,

00:01:52.778 --> 00:01:54.333
whereas when you try it
hot in a few minutes,

00:01:54.333 --> 00:01:57.003
you're going to find it's
basically just warm fat.

00:01:57.003 --> 00:01:58.884
- It melts like butter, but it's a liver,

00:01:58.884 --> 00:01:59.836
how is this happening?

00:01:59.836 --> 00:02:01.508
I thought I wouldn't like it by itself

00:02:01.508 --> 00:02:03.365
but I think it's seriously really good,

00:02:03.365 --> 00:02:04.619
just straight up by itself.

00:02:04.619 --> 00:02:06.082
- Do you think, is it
like melts in your mouth

00:02:06.082 --> 00:02:07.197
but not in your hands.

00:02:07.197 --> 00:02:08.357
- [Jason] No it'll melt in your hand.

00:02:08.357 --> 00:02:10.420
- Yeah what are doing Mike?

00:02:10.420 --> 00:02:12.467
- [Jason] This is the pan-seared foie gras

00:02:12.467 --> 00:02:15.416
with the Inca corn, the Sumo tangerines

00:02:15.416 --> 00:02:17.552
and Tandoori oil.

00:02:17.552 --> 00:02:20.111
- You know when it's cooked
it's a lot less creamy.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:23.364
- I think I like this
better than when it's like--

00:02:23.364 --> 00:02:24.478
- [Jason] Cold?

00:02:24.478 --> 00:02:26.637
- Yeah, I guess better
than when it's cold.

00:02:26.637 --> 00:02:28.979
- It tastes more meaty now.

00:02:28.979 --> 00:02:31.194
- You've made this seem very civilized.

00:02:31.194 --> 00:02:32.402
I kinda came into this thinking,

00:02:32.402 --> 00:02:36.790
it would be like people would
be like spitting food out

00:02:36.790 --> 00:02:38.044
and you know...

00:02:38.044 --> 00:02:40.227
- [Jason] This is with Yuzu Ponzu.

00:02:40.227 --> 00:02:42.572
So ponzu is just like acidulated soy sauce

00:02:42.572 --> 00:02:44.940
with a fresh yuzu juice,
which is a citrus,

00:02:44.940 --> 00:02:46.565
and some puffed rice on there for texture.

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:48.771
- It's like it's got Rice Krispies on it.

00:02:48.771 --> 00:02:50.466
(laughter)

00:02:50.466 --> 00:02:51.859
- Snap, crackle...

00:02:51.859 --> 00:02:52.997
foie!

00:02:52.997 --> 00:02:54.689
(laughter)

00:02:54.689 --> 00:02:56.394
- Dude.

00:02:56.394 --> 00:02:57.764
- This is good.
- This is rich.

00:02:57.764 --> 00:03:00.109
- (laughs) It's pure fat, man!

00:03:00.109 --> 00:03:01.665
- This is maybe too intense for me.

00:03:01.665 --> 00:03:02.547
- [Jason] Really?

00:03:02.547 --> 00:03:04.384
- Dude this is the best one by far.

00:03:04.384 --> 00:03:06.195
- This is so good.

00:03:06.195 --> 00:03:07.867
- But if you lied to me and told me,

00:03:07.867 --> 00:03:09.306
"This is a piece of steak."

00:03:09.306 --> 00:03:10.398
I would just be like,

00:03:10.398 --> 00:03:11.892
"This is the best steak I've ever had!"

00:03:11.892 --> 00:03:12.952
(laughter)

00:03:12.952 --> 00:03:15.171
- I don't mind the way it's produced

00:03:15.171 --> 00:03:17.702
because everything else we eat meat-wise

00:03:17.702 --> 00:03:21.301
is produced in a much worse
way that foie gras is.

00:03:21.301 --> 00:03:23.739
- I think what I thought was that

00:03:23.739 --> 00:03:25.202
what's happening, how Jason said,

00:03:25.202 --> 00:03:28.267
in some countries was
happening everywhere.

00:03:28.267 --> 00:03:30.241
So it's a little comforting to know that

00:03:30.241 --> 00:03:32.098
that's not the way that
they're all being treated.

00:03:32.098 --> 00:03:34.490
- You know, to eat meat, and I love meat,

00:03:34.490 --> 00:03:37.113
you have to not think about

00:03:37.113 --> 00:03:38.901
how it's prepared that much.

00:03:38.901 --> 00:03:40.271
Maybe a little too rich for me,

00:03:40.271 --> 00:03:44.556
that last dish, I was glad
it was my last one of the day

00:03:44.556 --> 00:03:47.252
because I think I need to
go take a nap after that.

00:03:47.252 --> 00:03:48.566
- What up, dude.

00:03:48.566 --> 00:03:50.627
- You know, Mardi Foie!

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.115
- Foie-dy Gras.

00:03:53.115 --> 00:03:54.049
- Get Foie-d!

00:03:54.469 --> 00:03:55.583
- Ok.

00:03:55.583 --> 00:03:57.325
You guys are out of control.

00:03:57.325 --> 00:03:58.677
- What the foie, Macy?

00:03:58.677 --> 00:04:00.092
(laughter)

